Compatible scalar complements are reused from the existing forward-diagram interval-basis result: regard the nested filtration layers as an all-forward inclusion diagram, append the quotient by the selected subspace, and use its homogeneous interval basis. The quotient distinguishes the killed basis intervals from those surviving in the quotient, giving a complement compatible with every layer. This does not reconstruct mixed-arrow natural endomorphisms and does not supply a new standalone scalar-complement result. The nearest open-question status is UNKNOWN; no originality or open-problem-resolution claim is made.
